B11: Talk to 2 cyebrsecurity experts from the industry

Objective

The goal of this activity is to gain insight into real-world cybersecurity work and current industry trends by speaking with cybersecurity professionals.

Method

I spoke with two cybersecurity professionals/experienced individuals involved in cybersecurity-related work and discussed the types of projects and security challenges they currently deal with.

Findings
Expert 1 – Security Awareness and Threat Prevention
The first discussion focused on common cybersecurity threats such as phishing attacks, password compromise, and social engineering. They explained how organisations increasingly rely on multi-factor authentication and user awareness training to reduce risks.
Expert 2 – Network Security and Monitoring
The second discussion focused on monitoring network activity and identifying suspicious behaviour. They explained how intrusion detection systems and continuous monitoring help organisations detect threats early and respond quickly.
Security Principle

These discussions reinforced:

Defence-in-depth strategies
Continuous monitoring and detection
Authentication and access control
Human awareness in cybersecurity
Evidence
Notes taken during the discussions
Informal conversations with cybersecurity-related professionals, tutors, or experienced individuals
Reflection summary of key cybersecurity topics discussed
Reflection

This activity provided insight into how cybersecurity concepts are applied in real environments. I learned that organisations combine technical controls with user education and monitoring systems to strengthen overall security.
